  "headline": "Nuwara Eliya: Little England, Alpine Gardens & High-Grown Ceylon Tea",
  "description": "Founded as a cool-climate retreat by British planters, Nuwara Eliya still has its red-brick post office, Tudor-style cottages, racecourse and rose gardens — all set among some of the highest tea estates in the world.\n\nI arrive by the scenic train, stay in heritage bungalows with log fires and open the doors of working factories, where the master tea-maker explains why high-grown leaf tastes so bright and delicate.",
